      "text": "Since $\\mathbf{A}^{-1}$ is the inverse of $\\mathbf{A},$\nwe have $\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\\mathbf{A} = \\mathbf{I}.$\nMultiplying this equation on the left by $\\mathbf{A}^2,\\$ we obtain\n$\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{I}\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{A}^2.$\nSince $\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\\mathbf{A} = \\mathbf{I},$\n$\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{I}\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{A}^2.$\nTherefore, the inverse of $\\mathbf{A}^2$ is $\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}}.$\nThe answer is: \\begin{pmatrix}2&5\\-1&-3\\end{pmatrix}",
