      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. **Understanding the Problem:**\n\n   We are given a $2 \\times 2$ matrix $\\mathbf{A}$ with the inverse $\\mathbf{A}^{-1}$, which is provided by the problem statement.\n   We need to find the inverse of $\\mathbf{A}^2$.\n\n2. **Matrix Property:**\n\n   Note that the inverse of $\\mathbf{A}^2$ is given by $(\\mathbf{A}^2)^{-1} = (\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2$.\n\n3. **Matrix Squaring:**\n\n   We need to compute the square of $\\mathbf{A}^{-1}$.\n\n   \\[\n   (\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2 = \\mathbf{A}^{-1} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^{-1}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Element-wise Calculation:**\n\n   Calculate each element of the resulting matrix.\n\n   Let \n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n   \n   For element at position $(1,1)$:\n   \\[\n   (A^{-1})_{11}^2 = a_{11}^2 = 2^2 = 4\n   \\]\n\n   For element at position $(1,2)$:\n   \\[\n   (A^{-1})_{12}^2 = a_{12}a_{21} = 5(-1) = -5\n   \\]\n\n   For element at position $(2,1)$:\n   \\[\n   (A^{-1})_{21}^2 = a_{21}a_{12} = (-1)(5) = -5\n   \\]\n\n   For element at position $(2,2)$:\n   \\[\n   (A^{-1})_{22}^2 = a_{22}^2 = (-3)^2 = 9\n   \\]\n\n5. **Construct the Resulting Matrix:**\n\n   Combining the above elements, we get:\n   \\[\n   (\\mathbf{A}^{-1})^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 9 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 4 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 9 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]\n\nThis is the inverse of $\\mathbf{A}^2$.",
